"Run T-301 again as a switchback: each city and operating hour gets the new rule or the old one at random, analysed with city and hour fixed effects. Over 14 days its power to detect the 1.8-minute gain is 100% (98% over 7 days), with 2% false wins when there is no gain. Carryover between hours shifts the estimate by only -0.02 minutes here; the larger gap to the per-order effect (-1.79) comes from weighting every city-hour equally, so weight blocks by orders when the decision is about orders."
